# Performance And Reliability

- Minimize blocking I/O. Database and external API work should be async when used from async request paths.
- Avoid N+1 database queries. Use explicit eager loading, joins, or batched queries for related data.
- Use the shared pagination contract for list endpoints that can grow; reuse `app.schemas.pagination` instead of creating new pagination models.
- Make transaction boundaries clear. Commit on successful request-scoped work and rollback on exceptions.
- Use row locks, advisory locks, unique constraints, or idempotent writes for flows that can race.
- Add caching only when the data access pattern and invalidation behavior are clear.
- Prefer lifespan context managers for application startup and shutdown work instead of `@app.on_event`.
